 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 547363,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "A researcher studying minnows, a type of fish, kept two groups of 20 fish in separate containers. The containers were linked by a pair of small tubes outfitted with a pump that constantly circulated water between both tanks. The researcher observed both groups of fish after placing a larger fish known to be a predator of minnows into one of the tanks. Fish in both tanks demonstrated alarm behavior. How can you explain these observations?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1074339,
     "content_html": "Fish in the tank that received the predator released alarm signals in chemical form. These compounds circulated and reached the other tank, eliciting an alarm response from the fish there nonetheless."
    },
    {
     "id": 1074340,
     "content_html": "Fish in the tank that received the predator released alarm signals in the form of electrical signals. These compounds circulated and reached the other tank, eliciting an alarm response from the fish there nonetheless."
    },
    {
     "id": 1074341,
     "content_html": "The predator introduced in one tank of fish released alarm signals in chemical form. These compounds circulated and reached the other tank, eliciting an alarm response from the fish there nonetheless."
    },
    {
     "id": 1074342,
     "content_html": "Fish in the tank that did not receive the predator released alarm signals in the chemical form. These compounds circulated and reached the other tank and elicited an alarm response from the fish."
    }
   ],
